Closes #19274
(cherry picked from commit c0688a2754c31d4ad89b3999f1ba0863601d47e0)

Backport notes (zfs-2.4.4): every conflict was in context from
master-only changes that zfs-2.4 does not have.  Resolved so the result
is c0688a275 minus those changes:
- dmu_impl.h, dmu.c, dmu_direct.c: 2.4 has no dsa_dio_verify_fails
  (3f94b2031, "Redo a Direct I/O write that fails verify from a private
  copy").  dmu_sync() and dmu_write_direct() set up dsa_waiters and
  dr_sync_arg, and set DR_IN_DMU_SYNC under db_mtx, as c0688a275 does.
- zil.c: zil_replay() keeps 2.4's replay buffer and has no split-write
  state (7c3d85aaf, "ZIL replay can apply part of a split WR_NEED_COPY
  write"); it gains only the TX_WRITE2 scan and its reset.
- zdb.c: 2.4 has no zdb_count_ddt_log_frees() (db78d8b07), so there is
  no call of it to update.
- dsl_scan.c, zfs_replay.c: copyright lines.
- common.run, Makefile.am: the four new tests join 2.4's lists, which
  lack master's split-write tests.
In each function c0688a275 changes, what still differs from master
after it comes from master-only changes unrelated to it.

